Upstream work credited in this repository
-----------------------------------------

No third-party source files are vendored here. The following public, Apache-2.0 work from the Kaggle competition
"Google Quantum AI - Verifiable Quantum Circuit Compilation" is re-implemented, loaded at run time, or read as data;
each use is also credited at the point of use in the code:

- scripts/d3_invsqrt_model.py re-implements the arithmetic of Syed Asad Ali's exact invsqrt model `whole_model.py`
  (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Syed Asad Ali). The author's code is not included or executed; the published model
  JSON is read as data.
- tools/dfthc-refit/dfthc_refit.py: the projected L-BFGS refit follows the idea of anazemcev's public Apache-2.0
  complete-H projected L-BFGS refit, re-implemented.
- tools/dfthc-refit loads Lera's (marculera) emitter `tensorqrom.py` (Apache-2.0) unmodified from a user-supplied
  directory at run time; it is not included. That emitter credits mrmeows' cached-product emitter and Heliosli's
  signed scratch. gauge.py adapts the emitter's borrowed-top-bit handling, as documented in gauge.py.
- scripts/chem_word_table_registry.json lists public chemistry word tables with their first public authors.
- The official verifiers and kickmix (Qualtran, Apache-2.0, Google LLC) are used but not included.
- tools/kmsim/kmsim.py is Asterios Panoras's kmsim (Apache-2.0), copied unmodified from the public QCC Atlas toolkit
  (https://www.kaggle.com/code/asteriospanoras/qcc-atlas-toolkit-in-notebook-chemistry-refit). It is a zero-dependency
  NumPy simulator for the kickmix text format, kept as an independent fallback checker.
